Now, Step 2 says to multiply the total pages by the number of problems per page. Each page has 9 problems, right? So 10 pages times 9 problems per page. Let me do that multiplication. 10 multiplied by 9 is 90. So that would mean she has 90 problems total. Hmm, that seems right. Let me check again.

Alternatively, maybe I can break it down. For math homework: 7 pages times 9 problems each. That would be 7*9=63. Then reading homework: 3 pages times 9 problems each. 3*9=27. Then add those two together: 63 +27. That also equals 90. Yep, same result. So both methods give me 90. So I think that's the correct answer.
