- **Dimes:** $5 \text{ piles} \times 3 \text{ coins/pile} = 15 \text{ dimes}$

Adding both amounts gives:  
$15 \text{ quarters} + 15 \text{ dimes} = 30 \text{ coins}$

Alternatively, since there are $5 + 5 = 10$ piles total and each pile has 3 coins:  
$10 \text{ piles} \times 3 \text{ coins/pile} = 30 \text{ coins}$

